  "notes": "{飛|と}び{散|ち}る is a compound verb combining {飛|と}ぶ (to fly) + {散|ち}る (to scatter). It vividly describes things flying apart in multiple directions.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pattern: Xが{飛|と}び{散|ち}る\n- No transitive pair\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{飛|と}び{散|ち}っている describes the resulting state — things are scattered about after flying apart.\n\nCOMMON SUBJECTS:\n- {水|みず}/{水滴|すいてき}が{飛|と}び{散|ち}る: water/droplets splatter\n- ガラスの{破片|はへん}が{飛|と}び{散|ち}る: glass shards scatter\n- {火花|ひばな}が{飛|と}び{散|ち}る: sparks fly\n- {血|ち}が{飛|と}び{散|ち}る: blood spatters\n\nUSAGE:\nConveys a dynamic, often sudden image. Common in both everyday descriptions (splashing water) and dramatic scenes (explosions, accidents).",
